▸ [F.1] A forwarded screenshot of R9's pass, shown after the wait, is refused; R9's live pass is accepted (a screenshot goes stale in under a minute, and even a fresh one can only be used once)
    · roster totp as desk-A stored it: step 30s, tolerance ±1 step(s), 6 digits
    · What this step proves: a screenshot goes stale in under a minute, and even a fresh one can only be used once. What it does NOT prove: that a forwarded QR is rejected. The desk accepts the code's step ±1 (a 90-second window around its own clock), so a screenshot forwarded and shown within 30–60 seconds of being taken DOES pass (longer if the desk's clock runs behind the phone's). That does not help an attacker: the code turns over every 30 seconds, so the screenshot is worthless within a minute, and a fresh one is worth exactly what the runner's own pass is worth: one claim on one record. Used by someone else it spends the runner's claim, not a new one — the runner is then refused "Already claimed" (5.1, 5.2), and if two offline desks both hand a pack over, that is the duplicate-collection case: the chain keeps one claim and the other desk flags it (6.1).
    · FOR WHOEVER FILMS THIS: take the screenshot, WAIT on camera until the desk would refuse it, present it, show the refusal. Do not cut the wait. Without the wait the clip shows a fresh screenshot being refused, which the product does not do — a fresh screenshot passes (see above). Then show the runner's own live pass being accepted at the next desk.
    · screenshot of R9's pass taken 2026-09-25T09:33:44.387Z (step 59677627); a desk on the same clock accepts it until 2026-09-25T09:34:29.000Z and refuses it from 2026-09-25T09:34:30.000Z
    · waiting 47.6s of real time (tolerance from the roster + 2s margin), no mocked clock
    · desk-A scans the screenshot 47.6s after it was taken: EXPIRED, screen shows bib 9
    · desk-B scans R9: GREEN, screen shows bib 9 (chain bib 9)
    · step took 48.4s, almost all of it the wait: the screenshot had to outlive the roster's ±1 step tolerance before it was shown
  ✓ PASS

